Note: The shape enforces [=CORE-02=]: at least one <code>dct:conformsTo</code> value must be a conformance class URI of this suite (the qualified value shape matching <code>https://specs.fairdatapoint.org/v&hellip;/conformance/&hellip;</code>), which simultaneously pins the specification version the deployment implements.

## Catalog metadata schema ## {#catalog-metadata}

<pre class=include>
path: ../src/tables/table-catalog-metadata.html
</pre>

The catalog metadata schema defined in SHACL:

<pre class=include-code>
path: ../src/rdf/shacl-catalog.ttl
highlight: turtle
</pre>

Since only the FDP's own record and <code>Catalog</code> records are mandatory, the metadata structure below the catalogs varies per deployment.
As the FDP is most commonly used to provide metadata of datasets, deployments typically also define <code>Dataset</code> and <code>Distribution</code> schemas following the DCAT model; deployments are free to replace these with custom schemas, as long as [=CORE-15=] is satisfied.
If other types of digital objects are used, the catalog metadata must contain the navigation information from the catalog to those records, per [[#navigation]].

# Requirements summary # {#requirements-summary}

<table class="def">
    <caption>FDP Core requirements</caption>
    <thead>
        <tr><th>ID</th><th>Level</th><th>Summary</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-01=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Root URL serves the FDP's own metadata record</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-02=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>FDP record declares implemented conformance classes via <code>dct:conformsTo</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-03=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>All other records reachable from at least one Catalog</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-04=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>GET on every record, container and schema returns 200 + representation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-05=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>HEAD supported wherever GET is</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-06=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>404 for unknown resources (410 MAY for deleted)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-07=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Turtle and JSON-LD available via content negotiation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-08=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Turtle is the default representation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-09=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>406 for unsatisfiable Accept headers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-10=]</td><td>SHOULD</td><td>ETag/Last-Modified and conditional requests</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-11=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Navigation information for every record that leads to other records</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-12=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Children listed via <code>ldp:contains</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-13=]</td><td>SHOULD</td><td>DirectContainer with <code>ldp:hasMemberRelation</code>/<code>ldp:membershipResource</code> when a domain predicate exists</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-14=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Schemas expressed in SHACL</td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-15=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Schema target class is (a subclass of) <code>dcat:Resource</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-16=]</td><td>SHOULD</td><td>Records reference their profile via <code>dct:conformsTo</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>[=CORE-17=]</td><td>MUST</td><td>Referenced profiles resolve to the SHACL schema</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

